    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93132" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σᾰλᾰμίς</span></b>  (also in Gramm. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σᾰλᾰμίν</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>, Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
			D.P.
			498
		</span></i>), gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῖνος</span>, ἡ, <u>Salamis</u>, an island and town of the same name,
		between Athens and Megara, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.557
		</span></i>, etc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a town of Cyprus
			founded by Teucer of Salamis, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				10.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.162
			</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαλαμίνη</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιφάνιος</span>
			.</div>
